# G054 — Grade Book

*v2. See `grade-book.md` for prose: student/course/assignment triples,
missing-grade semantics, GPA with optional missing-as-zero projection,
distribution histograms.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Term-End Report Cards

[term-end-reports @students @courses
    IN ORDER TO
        produce each student's transcript
        with both current and projected GPA
        reviewed by two parties before release

    for @student in @students
        @transcript <- {
            courses: for @c in @courses
                {id: @c:id,
                 average: [gb[course-average {student: @student:id, course: @c:id}]]
                 missing: [gb[missing        {student: @student:id, course: @c:id}]]}
            gpa:           [gb[gpa {student: @student:id}]]
            projected-gpa: [gb[gpa {student: @student:id, missing-as-zero?: true}]]
        }

        concurrent [
            <- @teacher{review transcript: @transcript}
            <- @advisor{flag risk in: @transcript}
        ]
        join

        @transcript
            where
                every course has no missing assignments
                and gpa equals projected-gpa
                    (otherwise missing grades are inflating the average)
                and both teacher and advisor reviews were received
            || -> #flag-for-attention
                student: @student
                reason: @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[gb
    new
    add-student      {student}
    add-course       {course}
    add-assignment   {assignment}
    record-grade     {student-id, assignment-id, points}
    grade-of         {student-id, assignment-id}         ;; || not-recorded
    course-average   {student-id, course-id, missing-as-zero?}
    gpa              {student-id, missing-as-zero?}
    class-average    {assignment-id}
    missing          {student-id, course-id?}
    distribution     {course-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: missing as option, not zero

[gb[grade-of {student-id: @s, assignment-id: @a}]
    || -> nil
    where
        missing grades surface as resistance, not as zero
        so that "hasn't submitted" and "submitted with zero" are distinguishable
]

The `|| -> nil` fulfillment lets callers treat absence as nil when
convenient; the resolver never silently substitutes zero.

---

## GPA as projection: current vs projected

[gb[gpa {student-id: @s}]
    where
        current GPA includes only recorded grades
        and missing-as-zero projection substitutes 0 for each missing grade
        so the gap between them measures "how much is the student's
        standing propped up by ungraded work"
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @gb <- [gb[new]]
    [gb[add-student {student: {id: 1, name: "Alice"}}]]
    [gb[add-course {course: {id: 101, name: "Algebra", credits: 3}}]]
    [gb[add-assignment {assignment: {id: 1001, course-id: 101,
                                       name: "HW1", max-points: 10}}]]
    [gb[add-assignment {assignment: {id: 1002, course-id: 101,
                                       name: "HW2", max-points: 10}}]]

    [gb[record-grade {student-id: 1, assignment-id: 1001, points: 9}]]

    -> [gb[course-average {student-id: 1, course-id: 101}]]
    ;; -> 0.9  (just HW1: 9/10)

    -> [gb[course-average {student-id: 1, course-id: 101,
                            missing-as-zero?: true}]]
    ;; -> 0.45  (HW1=9, HW2=0; avg = 9/20)

    -> [gb[missing {student-id: 1, course-id: 101}]]
    ;; -> [{id: 1002, name: "HW2"}]
]
